    "rationale": "The exhaustive optimizer-free V15/R13 audit completed all 12518 start phases and reduced required-safety failures from 2779 to 380, with 79 hard impacts, 291 hard-ROM cases, 40 joint-safety cases and 40 joint-velocity cases; effort, fall, forbidden contact, self-collision, world escape and non-finite failures were zero. Every hard-ROM event was terminal ankle-pitch plantarflexion, and failed references clustered at the retained minus-thirty-degree solve bound. The immutable ankle hard limit is minus forty degrees, so V15 retained only ten degrees of reference reserve while the existing corpus contract and measured 11.33-degree reference-to-peak transient support a fifteen-degree target. This identity preserves every V15 source, split, crop, timing, BodySchema, USD, PD, contact, safety, ground-seating, sole-pitch and sole-roll setting. After the V15 solve it raises the final bilateral ankle-pitch floor to minus twenty-five degrees, providing 261800 microradians of hard-limit reserve. Each ankle transfer is removed exactly from knee and hip pitch, preserving the summed sagittal chain command while respecting their existing lower bounds. The required transfer is expanded through a thirty-two-pass symmetric constrained temporal envelope; a second constrained envelope prefers the adjacent knee and uses hip pitch only around intervals where knee margin is exhausted, minimizing non-commutative interaction with hip roll. A complete twenty-seven-artifact diagnostic measured a worst ankle-pitch acceleration of 12297600 microradians per second squared versus 81824400 for pointwise clipping and the frozen 25000000 admission limit, without exceeding the twenty-five-percent reference velocity reserve. This remains data-only remediation: optimizer execution is forbidden until fresh deterministic import, native pose, formal visual and exhaustive zero-safety dynamic evidence all pass."
